ions include Play T2. So the action would be Play T2. \n\nBut let me double-check. The hand has T2 as a single tile. Discarding it doesn't help others form sequences. So it's a safe discard. \n\nTherefore, the answer is Play T2.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand has multiple tiles in T suit (T2, T4, T5, T6, T7, T8) and W9 pair. Discarding T2, a single tile not part of any sequence, minimizes risk of aiding opponents while preserving potential for forming T4-5-6 or other sequences.  \nReason: T2 is isolated and not part of any existing or potential sequences. Discarding it avoids giving others a tile to complete a meld and maintains flexibility for future draws.  \nAnswer: Play T2"}
