erefore, the best move is to play T8.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing T8 allows forming a chow of T6, T7, T8, completing a third meld. This strengthens the hand structure and aligns with the All Chows pattern, while the pair of W9s (terminals) contributes to the Outside Hand pattern. Combined, these patterns could reach the minimum 8-point threshold if additional scoring elements are present.  \nReason: Forming the T6-T7-T8 chow adds a critical meld, improving the hand's structure and increasing the likelihood of meeting the 8-point requirement. Playing T8 is a strategic step toward a winning hand.  \nAnswer: Play T8"}
